# q35ro: the dense Qwen3.8-27B (qwen35, Body35) verify pass of k rows reads its dense FFN and its head once for all rows. Measured
# before (dspine-verify-k outcome, A6000, bench_verify_rows): c_v(2) 1.6627, c_v(4) 2.9974, c_v(8) 5.6750 at depth 6, step 27.564
# ms, about 0.67 step a row: the per-slot `_sel` FFN and the per-row head re-read 17.5 ms of bytes a row [derived, 11.41 GB at
# 653 GB/s]. After, those terms grow by the read-once m-column cores' t_m/t_1 (fewrow outcome, A6000): Q4_K at k 17408 1.30 /
# 1.84 / 2.84, Q6_K down 1.33 / 1.74 / 2.49, head 1.02 / 1.66 / 2.36 at m = 2 / 4 / 8. With gate/up 9.83 ms, down 6.05 ms and head
# 1.6 ms a read, and the rest of the pass taken from the before cells (c_v(k) x step - k x 17.5 ms: 10.8 / 12.6 / 16.4 ms), plus
# 0.27 ms of added launches: c_v(2) = (10.8 + 22.3 + 0.27) / 27.56 = 1.21, c_v(4) = (12.6 + 31.6 + 0.3) / 27.56 = 1.61,
# c_v(8) = (16.4 + 48.0 + 0.3) / 27.56 = 2.35 [derived]. Band +-10 %: c_v(2) 1.10..1.33 (the judged cell, depth 6), c_v(4)
# 1.45..1.77 and c_v(8) 2.1..2.6 as co-rows. Base and head run back to back, each under its own lease (two binaries; this is a
# profile, not an interleaved A/B: the effect predicted, -27 % at k = 2, is far past a window's ~5 % drift).
kind: profile
question: does the 27B verify pass of 2 to 8 rows cost what the read-once cores' measured column ratios say, once its dense FFN and
  head read their weights once?
term: c_v(k) = median wall of step_rows::<k> / median wall of one plain step, k = 2, 4, 8, depths 6 and 4096, batch 1, graph
  replay, RTX A6000 (bench_verify_rows), this tree's c_v(2) at depth 6 judged
unit: ratio
predict: 1.10..1.33
condition: bench-verify-rows.sh holds the lease for each run; the base tree (main + the bench) runs first, then this tree, both
  on /models/Qwen3.8-27B/Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_K_M.gguf; the base's c_v(2) must read 1.66 +- 3 % (the dspine outcome) or the window
  is suspect; every verify rows record carries its spread, a cell above 3 % is read again
decide-in: the read-once verify costs what the cores say: keep q35ro; the next term for DSpine and MTP is c_v(8) (2.35 predicted
  against the 1.3 the DSpine plan wants), which a few-row MMA (ncu of q4k_gemv_mcol first) would lower
decide-below: c_v(2) under 1.10: the m-column cores cost less in the pass than in the bench (L2 reuse across the gate and up
  launches); re-fit the fewrow-based model before pricing the MMA round
decide-above: c_v(2) over 1.33: the unfused path's launches, copies or the SwiGLU cost more than 0.27 ms, or the head did not
  become one launch; read the pass in nsys (tools/ref/nsys-gpu.sh) per entry before any keep decision
# Outcome (2026-11-16, A6000 300 W, bench-verify-rows.sh under the lease, base = main 7d0a62e7b with the dspine bench
#  (67d92709d, ac4e962d6) cherry-picked, head = q35ro with the same; medians of 5, spread <= 0.73 %): c_v(2) at depth 6 is
#  1.2089 (base 1.6623, the dspine outcome's 1.6627 within 0.03 %): decide-in. Base / head c_v(2, 4, 8): depth 6 1.6623 /
#  2.9868 / 5.6641 -> 1.2089 / 1.6201 / 2.4007; depth 4096 1.6696 / 3.0034 / 5.6948 -> 1.2225 / 1.6595 / 2.4954. The plain
#  step 27.619 -> 27.565 ms at depth 6, 28.273 -> 28.241 at 4096. Predicted 1.21 / 1.61 / 2.35: the fewrow column ratios carry
#  into the pass. c_v(8) 2.40 is the next term (the DSpine plan wants 1.3): the m-column cores' own growth past two columns.
